WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.490
- All right, so we have
time for just one more story

00:00:02.490 --> 00:00:05.488
on this Martin Luther King Jr
Day, this is "What I'm Liking"

00:00:05.488 --> 00:00:08.670
(upbeat music)

00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:11.460
Last year I shared the
story of four teenage girls

00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:14.280
from Pennsylvania who fought
their school's book Ban.

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:17.250
The District had pulled
books on race and diversity

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:20.400
including a children's book on Rosa Parks.

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:22.680
- Even with the discrimination
I faced being here

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:24.630
and living here for 17 years

00:00:24.630 --> 00:00:28.500
never have I encountered
this blatant discrimination

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:30.960
against all people of
different orientation.

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:33.840
- No one thought that we would
have any impact on the world

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:36.120
but this experience showed us
that our voice does matter.

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:37.902
Like, we were the change.

00:00:37.902 --> 00:00:39.901
(audience cheering)
- Yeah,

00:00:39.901 --> 00:00:41.220
the teens were successful

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:44.130
and the band was
reversed, which is so rad.

00:00:44.130 --> 00:00:45.270
This week the King Center

00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:47.610
in Atlanta is recognizing
their amazing work

00:00:47.610 --> 00:00:50.610
with a beloved community
youth influencer award.

00:00:50.610 --> 00:00:52.800
Two of the four ladies
are back with us today.

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:54.621
Everybody say hi to Edah and Olivia.

00:00:54.621 --> 00:00:56.707
(audience cheering)

00:00:56.707 --> 00:00:57.540
Hi y'all!

00:00:58.980 --> 00:01:00.390
- Hi.
- Hello.

00:01:00.390 --> 00:01:01.223
- Oh my God.

00:01:01.223 --> 00:01:03.150
So congrats Edah, on the award.

00:01:03.150 --> 00:01:05.070
A lot has happened since
I last spoke to you.

00:01:05.070 --> 00:01:06.300
So tell us about that.

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:08.520
- Yeah, so ever since the ban was reversed

00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:11.160
it's just been a crazy
journey for all of us.

00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:13.410
Christina, Olivia and I have now,

00:01:13.410 --> 00:01:14.520
we are now in college.

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:16.350
I attend the university at Pittsburgh

00:01:16.350 --> 00:01:18.540
since the ban was
reversed, we've just been

00:01:18.540 --> 00:01:21.930
in this crazy loop of like,
reaching out and talking

00:01:21.930 --> 00:01:24.540
and helping people that are
going through the same thing.

00:01:24.540 --> 00:01:28.650
Olivia and Christina went to
talk to Congress and Christina

00:01:28.650 --> 00:01:32.700
and I also were given the
opportunity to have a TED Talk

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:34.980
at the University of Pennsylvania.

00:01:34.980 --> 00:01:37.350
So the whole journey has been so crazy

00:01:37.350 --> 00:01:39.060
and now we are so humbled

00:01:39.060 --> 00:01:42.547
and honored to be accepting
this award from the King Center.

00:01:42.547 --> 00:01:44.700
(audience cheering)
- It's so incredibly cool.

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:46.590
Y'all are incredibly cool.

00:01:46.590 --> 00:01:48.630
Olivia, you're also helping other students

00:01:48.630 --> 00:01:50.280
around the country. That's right?

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:54.300
- Yes. There has unfortunately
only been an explosion

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:58.740
of book bans since we
reversed our book ban.

00:01:58.740 --> 00:02:02.130
So they've actually been
mainly targeting LGBTQ+

00:02:02.130 --> 00:02:06.390
youth and LGBTQ+ resources, right now.

00:02:06.390 --> 00:02:08.700
So we have been given
the opportunity to speak

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:11.130
to so many different school districts.

00:02:11.130 --> 00:02:13.410
We've been on many educational panels

00:02:13.410 --> 00:02:17.340
and our goal is to really
help others have that format

00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:19.830
so that they can fight back
against these book bans.

00:02:19.830 --> 00:02:22.802
- Absolutely. Thank you so much, ladies.

00:02:22.802 --> 00:02:24.678
(audience cheering)

00:02:24.678 --> 00:02:26.580
I have never even gotten
to hug y'all in person

00:02:26.580 --> 00:02:28.290
but I'm hugging you right now virtually.

00:02:28.290 --> 00:02:29.550
I love you guys so much.

00:02:29.550 --> 00:02:31.800
I, you just make me so
hopeful for the future.

00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:34.380
Y'all are incredibly gifted
young ladies and just

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:35.940
and very inspiring and powerful.

00:02:35.940 --> 00:02:37.590
So thank you for joining us, again.

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:40.300
I'm liking your post right now. Right?

00:02:40.300 --> 00:02:41.790
(Olivia laughing)

00:02:41.790 --> 00:02:43.170
And that's not all ladies.

00:02:43.170 --> 00:02:45.600
Our season-long partner
Pilot Pen, makers of FriXion,

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:47.520
the go-to a erase pen of
the Kelly Clarkson Show,

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:48.656
Want to celebrate people

00:02:48.656 --> 00:02:51.630
like you who are continuing the legacy

00:02:51.630 --> 00:02:52.800
of Martin Luther King Jr.

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:55.950
So they're donating a thousand
dollars to the King Center

00:02:55.950 --> 00:02:58.798
for Non-Violent Social
Justice on your behalf.

00:02:58.798 --> 00:03:00.873
(Audience cheering)
Thank you ladies.

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:04.480
Thank you so much to
all of our guests today,

00:03:04.480 --> 00:03:05.649
(audience cheering)
Cedric the Entertainer,

00:03:05.649 --> 00:03:09.420
Pam Grier, Quest Love, Veda
Tunstall and Bernice King.

00:03:09.420 --> 00:03:10.643
Let's remember on this Martin Luther Day,

00:03:10.643 --> 00:03:14.640
to be understanding of
one another and show grace

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:17.220
and empathy towards each
other and have great day,

00:03:17.220 --> 00:03:19.220
And if it's not, well try and change it.

